{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QEFm7giXbNw1eejRpTTnLR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The \"just over\" boundary tests use ±0.01 oz (≈0.28 g) and 6.0 oz — well outside a sub-milligram rounding gap. So an inclusive tolerance matching the gram figure's stated precision (0.001 g = 1e-6 kg) fixes the contradiction without making any genuinely-over car legal. This is the developer's GREEN fix for the confirmed WI5-ADV-001 finding. Let me apply it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":71132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1163},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f","uuid":"32afda8f-d791-4c95-80b0-4bf9be700feb","request_id":"req_011CbepSs4qcZhXqDHVgehDX"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QEFm7giXbNw1eejRpTTnLR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017juP1e4JZ3wL49FQYK3DmB","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/src/pinewood_derby/engine.py","old_string":"_MAX_MASS = Mass.from_ounces(5.0)  # M_max, the BSA weight limit (AC-W2)","new_string":"_MAX_MASS = Mass.from_ounces(5.0)  # M_max, the BSA weight limit (AC-W2)\n# AC-W2 names the limit two ways — 5.0 oz and (141.748 g) — and treats them as the\n# SAME quantity. Converting 5.0 oz gives 0.1417475 kg, but the gram figure the AC\n# equally endorses is 0.141748 kg, so a car weighed to exactly 141.748 g would fall\n# just outside a strict 5.0-oz threshold. The gap is < 0.001 g — purely an artifact\n# of stating the gram figure to three decimals. Compare inclusively within that\n# rounding precision so both named representations of the limit agree at the boundary\n# (WI5-ADV-001). The tolerance is far smaller than any real over-weight margin (the\n# boundary tests probe ≥ 0.01 oz ≈ 0.28 g over), so genuinely over-weight cars stay\n# illegal.\n_WEIGHT_LIMIT_TOL_KG = 1e-6  # 0.001 g — the precision AC-W2's gram figure is stated to"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":71132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1163},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f","uuid":"497e4aa5-ce93-4228-8037-863c3387eea7","request_id":"req_011CbepSs4qcZhXqDHVgehDX"}
