{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LEK6RX17MruAUkd6e3C8vd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full, honest picture, and it's decisive:\n\n- **WI-4 escalated** — hit *both* the developer attempt cap (6) and the adversarial cap (3), with 2 reproducible high findings still open at rev 3 (stall-on-incline DNF blows the <5ms perf NFR; same defect class via a second trigger).\n- **WI-5 escalated** — hit the adversarial cap (3) with a reproducible high finding open at rev 3 (stable, optimally-placed light cars wrongly reported as a crash; energy ledger non-closure).\n- **WI-6 incomplete** — crashed mid dev-attempt 5, with open high findings (absolute-distance stability cliff; placement \"head-start\" injecting fake kinetic energy and corrupting the energy ledger).\n- **WI-7…WI-13 never started** (wheels, aero, friction, alignment, energy closure, priority-order invariant, NFRs).\n- A recurring deep domain defect — **the energy ledger doesn't close and `pe_initial` omits the transition arc** — persisted unresolved across WI-4/WI-5/WI-6 adversarial loops. That's exactly what the currently-failing AC-E4 test (`0.029 < 0.001`) is.\n\nThis is a genuine escalation, and the factory's own rule is explicit: *hitting a loop cap → escalate to the user, never silent pass; don't silence your critics.* Two work items hit caps and the run never reached PO sign-off. Forcing a sign-off by hand-fixing the physics myself would violate that protective-gate design (and conflate the developer and PO roles). Repeated resumes also keep crashing on the same flaky StructuredOutput failure (5×) and won't un-escalate WI-4/WI-5.\n\nSo the correct, spec-compliant terminal state is **escalated**. Let me compute precise metrics from the transcripts and assemble the run-record."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":239,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6385,"cache_read_input_tok