egal_weight gram-boundary, HIGH) was fixed during continuation.\n  WI-6  Weight placement (d_COM) ....................... INTERRUPTED (crash, not a gate)\n          • dev attempt 5 ended without structured output (infra failure, 5th occurrence)\n          • open HIGH findings unresolved: placement \"head-start\" injects fake kinetic energy\n            and corrupts the energy ledger (WI6-ADV-002/003).\n  WI-7..WI-13  wheels, aero, friction, alignment, energy-closure,\n               priority-order invariant (AC-ED1), NFRs .. NOT STARTED\n\nRECURRING ROOT DEFECT (the human decision this escalates)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nAcross WI-4/WI-5/WI-6 the adversarial reviewer repeatedly surfaced the SAME class of\ndomain-correctness defect that the developer could not close within the caps:\n  • the energy ledger does not close to AC-E1 tolerance; reported pe_initial omits the\n    transition-arc descent (WI5-ADV-002/003/005/006, WI6-ADV-002/003); and\n  • the stall / DNF model is physically wrong (light-but-stable cars flagged as crashes;\n    stalled cars grind the 60s guard).\nThis is the live signature of the one currently-FAILING test on disk:\n  tests/test_engine_weight_wi5.py::test_ace4_w_gravity_matches_analytic_pe_drop_at_fine_dt\n  (AC-E4: w_gravity vs analytic PE drop — 2.9% error vs the 0.1% tolerance). WI-6's engine\n  changes regressed it; resolving it is the same physics work the loop escalated, so it was\n  left red rather than papered over.\n\nON-DISK STATE: 220 passing tests, 1 failing (the AC-E4 regression above), ruff clean,\nmypy --strict clean, coverage 97% overall / 98% engine. NO test files were modified to pass.\n\nRECOMMENDED NEXT STEP (human): re-scope WI-5/WI-6 energy-ledger + DNF physics as a focused\nfix (close the ledger incl. the transition arc; make the stall/DNF model physical), then\nre-run the build-loop for WI-6..WI-13. The protective gates worked as designed — this is a\ngenuine physics-correctness escalation, not a process failure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4206,"cache_read_input_tokens":124256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4206},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f","uuid":"cf9ff247-0fab-489d-ba68-f7f1ac1c4fa4","request_id":"req_011Cbf7Qy4v766hRpyfsroYr"}
