ne/TRD.html\",\n  \"backlog_ref\": null,\n  \"summary_ref\": null,\n  \"run_record_refs\": [],\n  \"changeset_refs\": [],\n  \"open_questions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"q1\",\n      \"question\": \"Confirm/replace the geometry constants (A4) and frontal-area defaults (A5).\",\n      \"resolved\": true,\n      \"resolution\": \"User accepted the Planner's BSA-typical documented defaults (R_outer 0.595 in, bore-based R_inner placeholder, r_axle 0.045 in nail shank, wheelbase 4.375 in, frontal area approx 1.75 in x 2.5 in). Each lands in constants.py with a sourced comment; R_inner stays a flagged placeholder, tunable if a magnitude looks off. Behavioral ACs remain direction-based so they hold under any reasonable values.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"q2\",\n      \"question\": \"Confirm the DNF-vs-penalty choice (A2).\",\n      \"resolved\": true,\n      \"resolution\": \"User confirmed: an unstable car (d_COM < 0.625 in, front normal force collapses) is a DNF with race_time_s = None (hard crash), returning the partial trajectory and the energy ledger up to the failure. Models the rear-bias tradeoff as a legible cliff rather than a finite penalty.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Rename the feature id to reflect broadened scope, or keep 0001-weight-placement-engine?\",\n      \"resolved\": true,\n      \"resolution\": \"User chose to rename: directory/id is now 0001-physics-engine to match the broadened full-physics scope. All internal references (feature.json, PRD/TRD, physics-spec appendix) updated; planning session_id unchanged.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"build\": {\n    \"session_id\": \"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f\",\n    \"log\": \"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/features/0001-physics-engine/build.log\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-06-02T10:03:30.197792+00:00\",\n    \"pid\": 10071\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":7,"newStart":6,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"status\": \"escalated\",","   \"description\": \"Pure, deterministic, dependency-free physics engine: given a full car design (weight, center-of-mass, wheels/rotational inertia, body drag, axle friction, alignment) and a validated track, time-step integrate the run and return a RaceResult (time, outcome, speeds, normal forces, and a closing energy ledger). Grounded in docs/physics-spec.md. No UI. First end-to-end exercise of the TDD build loop. (Scope broadened from weight+placement to full physics per PO decisions 2026-06-02; id renamed weight-placement-engine -> physics-engine 2026-06-02 to match scope.)\",","   \"created_at\": \"2026-06-02T00:00:00Z\",","-  \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:58:45.007359+00:00\",","+  \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T21:06:34.145251+00:00\",","   \"planning\": {","     \"session_id\": \"8c2a3e99-0ec2-4003-ad50-2335cc6befe9\"","   },"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
