{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014kQdQfXDj4L2VCarAwngYx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PuAooWSBjLkY6AkJNprwKL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/ericburdett/.claude/projects/-Users-ericburdett-Projects/memory/agentic-sdlc-factory.md","old_string":"NEXT (build order §10, step 1): run the **planner** to produce the first PRD/TRD for the derby sim\n(suggest the pure physics engine — weight + placement — as the first vertical slice), get user\napproval, then launch `workflows/build-loop.mjs`. First real run also tests the discovery symlink.","new_string":"DONE (2026-06-02): first real **build-loop** run of `0001-physics-engine` completed and\n**ESCALATED** (run-record `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json`;\nhuman summary `features/0001-physics-engine/ESCALATION.md`). Discovery symlink works. PO\ndecomposed into **13 work items**; WI-1..3 passed, WI-4 & WI-5 hit loop caps (escalated), WI-6\ninterrupted, WI-7..13 never started. Protective gates worked as designed: the adversarial\nreviewer repeatedly caught a real unresolved physics defect — the **energy ledger doesn't close\n/ `pe_initial` omits the transition arc**, and the **stall/DNF model is wrong** (light stable\ncars flagged as crashes; stalled cars grind the 60s guard → blows the <5ms NFR). On-disk: 220\ntests pass, 1 red (AC-E4, the ledger defect's signature — left red, not papered over). args note:\nbuild-loop needs prdRef/trdRef/profileRef as a real JSON object (a stringified args bails at\nvalidation). Two eval-loop signals: (a) recurring **\"subagent completed without calling\nStructuredOutput\"** crash (5×) on long physics-dev sessions; (b) the full suite runs each green\ngate, so a later WI's edit can regress an earlier WI's accepted test (WI-6 regressed WI-5 AC-E4).\n\nNEXT: human decision on the escalation — re-scope WI-5/WI-6 energy-ledger + DNF physics as a\nfocused fix, get the suite green, then re-run the build-loop for WI-6..WI-13. After a clean\nbuild, run `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (auditors + synthesizer) to populate audits/changesets."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":145012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"output_tokens":61,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f","uuid":"7464085b-e6f9-41df-8448-3fcb2377596b","request_id":"req_011Cbf7e1pEPAMZ5DSJ4rjw8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PuAooWSBjLkY6AkJNprwKL","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ericburdett/.claude/projects/-Users-ericburdett-Projects/memory/agentic-sdlc-factory.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f","uuid":"d3dc9dae-93be-4a49-a701-66f7f34e6edc","timestamp":"2026-06-02T21:07:26.512Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/ericburdett/.claude/projects/-Users-ericburdett-Projects/memory/agentic-sdlc-factory.md","oldString":"NEXT (build order §10, step 1): run the **planner** to produce the first PRD/TRD for the derby sim\n(suggest the pure physics engine — weight + placement — as the first vertical slice), get user\napproval, then launch `workflows/build-loop.mjs`. First real run also tests the discovery symlink.","newString":"DONE (2026-06-02): first real **build-loop** run of `0001-physics-engine` completed and\n**ESCALATED** (run-record `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json`;\nhuman summary `features/0001-physics-engine/ESCALATION.md`). Discovery symlink works. PO\ndecomposed into **13 work items**; WI-1..3 passed, WI-4 & WI-5 hit loop caps (escalated), WI-6\ninterrupted, WI-7..13 never started. Protective gates worked as designed: the adversarial\nreviewer repeatedly caught a real unresolved physics defect — the **energy ledger doesn't close\n/ `pe_initial` omits the transition arc**, and the **stall/DNF model is wrong** (light stable\ncars flagged as crashes; stalled cars grind the 60s guard → blows the <5ms NFR). On-disk: 220\ntests pass, 1 red (AC-E4, the ledger defect's signature — left red, not papered over). args note:\nbuild-loop needs prdRef/trdRef/profileRef as a real JSON object (a stringified args bails at\nvalidation). Two eval-loop signals: (a) recurring **\"subagent completed without calling\nStructuredOutput\"** crash (5×) on long physics-dev sessions; (b) the full suite runs each green\ngate, so a later WI's edit can regress an earlier WI's accepted test (WI-6 regressed WI-5 AC-E4).\n\nNEXT: human decision on the escalation — re-scope WI-5/WI-6 energy-ledger + DNF physics as a\nfocused fix, get the suite green, then re-run the build-loop for WI-6..WI-13. After a clean\nbuild, run `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (auditors + synthesizer) to populate audits/changesets.","originalFile":"---\nname: agentic-sdlc-factory\ndescription: \"Ongoing design of a self-improving multi-agent SDLC \\\"factory\\\" at ~/Projects/agentic-sdlc\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 800a79a5-f568-48d8-aee9-a453e54892c9\n---\n\nThe user is designing a **self-improving SDLC \"factory\"** — a deterministic multi-agent workflow\nthat builds apps (planner → PRD/TRD → TDD build loop → adversarial review → PO sign-off) and then\naudits *how it built* the feature to auto-improve its own agents/prompts/skills/hooks.\n\nLives at `~/Projects/agentic-sdlc/` (NOT a git repo yet). Full design in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\nKey decisions already made (see §11 decisions log there before re-deriving):\n- **Factory ⇄ products** separation; every learning has a **scope** (app-specific / archetype /\n  factory-general) = \"planes\" projected onto each lever (skill/hook/prompt/agent/workflow).\n- **Two-tier eval:** per-agent **auditor** (objective, observe-not-prescribe, always-on) →\n  **synthesizer** (correlates, classifies scope+blast-radius, emits auto-applied changeset).\n- **Guardrails:** commit every change (revertible); blast-radius tiering; protective agents (PO,\n  adversarial) never tuned toward leniency (\"don't silence your critics\"); synthesizer reads the\n  corpus not a single run.\n- Improvements **auto-apply** (no human review) — user's explicit choice; recoverability via\n  commits substitutes for review.\n\nArtifacts done: `charters/*.md` (7 role rubrics), `schema/run-record.schema.json`,\n`apps/_TEMPLATE/profile.md`, `gates.md` (definition-of-done + verdict schema per step — the\ncontrol-flow contract, distinct from charter rubrics), and the two workflow scripts\n`workflows/build-loop.mjs` + `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (drafted, not yet run). First app chosen:\n**pinewood-derby-sim** (frontend; TS/React/Vitest; teaches kids derby physics; educational\naccuracy is a hard requirement) at `apps/pinewood-derby-sim/profile.md`.\n\nDecisions: v1 builds work items **sequentially** (shared codebase; parallel-worktree is later).\n**First app is Python 3.12 via uv** (pytest/ruff/mypy; NO Node anywhere; `uv run <cmd>` is the\ncommand pattern in the profile) — engine-first, pure physics engine, pygame UI deferred; archetype\n`desktop-app`.\n\nDONE: 7 agent defs in `agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents/` (wrap charters; tools scoped — auditor/\nsynthesizer read-only). `git init` + baseline commit done. Python venv + tooling installed and all\n3 gate commands verified passing on the scaffold. Agent discovery wired via symlink\n`~/Projects/.claude/agents → agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents` — **UNVERIFIED until a workflow runs**\n(cwd project root is ~/Projects, not the factory).\n\nNEXT (build order §10, step 1): run the **planner** to produce the first PRD/TRD for the derby sim\n(suggest the pure physics engine — weight + placement — as the first vertical slice), get user\napproval, then launch `workflows/build-loop.mjs`. First real run also tests the discovery symlink.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":41,"oldLines":6,"newStart":41,"newLines":20,"lines":[" `~/Projects/.claude/agents → agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents` — **UNVERIFIED until a workflow runs**"," (cwd project root is ~/Projects, not the factory)."," ","-NEXT (build order §10, step 1): run the **planner** to produce the first PRD/TRD for the derby sim","-(suggest the pure physics engine — weight + placement — as the first vertical slice), get user","-approval, then launch `workflows/build-loop.mjs`. First real run also tests the discovery symlink.","+DONE (2026-06-02): first real **build-loop** run of `0001-physics-engine` completed and","+**ESCALATED** (run-record `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json`;","+human summary `features/0001-physics-engine/ESCALATION.md`). Discovery symlink works. PO","+decomposed into **13 work items**; WI-1..3 passed, WI-4 & WI-5 hit loop caps (escalated), WI-6","+interrupted, WI-7..13 never started. Protective gates worked as designed: the adversarial","+reviewer repeatedly caught a real unresolved physics defect — the **energy ledger doesn't close","+/ `pe_initial` omits the transition arc**, and the **stall/DNF model is wrong** (light stable","+cars flagged as crashes; stalled cars grind the 60s guard → blows the <5ms NFR). On-disk: 220","+tests pass, 1 red (AC-E4, the ledger defect's signature — left red, not papered over). args note:","+build-loop needs prdRef/trdRef/profileRef as a real JSON object (a stringified args bails at","+validation). Two eval-loop signals: (a) recurring **\"subagent completed without calling","+StructuredOutput\"** crash (5×) on long physics-dev sessions; (b) the full suite runs each green","+gate, so a later WI's edit can regress an earlier WI's accepted test (WI-6 regressed WI-5 AC-E4).","+","+NEXT: human decision on the escalation — re-scope WI-5/WI-6 energy-ledger + DNF physics as a","+focused fix, get the suite green, then re-run the build-loop for WI-6..WI-13. After a clean","+build, run `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (auditors + synthesizer) to populate audits/changesets."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
