 (`test_ace4_..._pe_drop`, AC-E4, 2.9% vs 0.1% tolerance) **is** the escalated ledger defect's signature; I left it red rather than paper over it. On disk: **220 pass / 1 fail, ruff clean, mypy --strict clean, 97% coverage.**\n\n**Artifacts written & validated:**\n- `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json` — schema-valid; `status: escalated`, 13 work-items with per-item findings/states, 42 adversarial findings (17 high), 11 rework loops, `loop_cap_hit: true`, `audits: []` (auditing is the eval-loop's job).\n- `feature.json` — `status: escalated`, `metrics_rollup` set, run-record ref appended, `summary_ref` → the new `ESCALATION.md` (human-readable why + recommended next step). Schema-valid.\n- `ESCALATION.md` — full breakdown for whoever picks this up.\n\n**Two signals worth feeding the eval-loop later:** (a) the *\"subagent completed without calling StructuredOutput\"* crash recurred 5× on the long physics-dev sessions; (b) the full suite runs at each green gate, so a later work item's edit silently regressed an earlier accepted test (WI-6 broke WI-5's AC-E4).\n\n**Recommended next step (your call):** re-scope the WI-5/WI-6 energy-ledger + DNF physics as a focused fix to get the suite green, then re-run the build-loop for WI-6…WI-13. I can do that, or attempt another workflow resume — but resuming won't un-escalate WI-4/WI-5 and keeps hitting the same crash, so a targeted fix first is the better path. Want me to take a pass at the energy-ledger fix?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":145268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":966},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8232da30-2be5-4a2b-b6c9-037553d88b1f","uuid":"8a9f3367-bef3-4d16-a421-88595da8b9dc","request_id":"req_